	quest.65D7F64025F490BE.quest_desc: [
		"&3Aluminium&r must be produced via advanced electrolysis in the &bElectrolytic Cell&r multiblock. This process uses Alumina Dust, Coke Dust, Carbon Rods, Aluminium Fluoride, and Molten Cryolite. It's important to note that the recipe requires a minimum quantity of 5760mB of Molten Cryolite and 432mB of Aluminium Fluoride to run. But these two ingredients are gradually consumed over the course of many recipes."
		""
		"On average, producing enough &3Liquid Aluminium&r for &e100 ingots&r will consume 432mB of Aluminium Fluoride and 432mB of Molten Cryolite."
	]
